# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values you need. TabFleet loads .env.local on launch
# (before any module reads process.env). Shell env vars still win over this file.

# ─── TextChest ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A profile uses TextChest when it has a Site:X column with "smscode=textchest:API-KEY[:parser]"
# and an "SMS Number" column.
#
# Defaults from TextChest's own REST docs:
#   Base: https://api.textchest.com/sms (textchest-async adds async_inbox=true)
#   Auth: HTTP Basic — API key as the username, empty password
#   Response: JSON array of { msg, ts, from }, newest first
# TabFleet sends number=<digits-only> and limit=10, then extracts the code from the newest msg.
# Override only if TextChest changes the base URL:
# TABFLEET_TEXTCHEST_URL=https://api.textchest.com/sms

# ─── Automatiq ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# For "password=automatiq:API-TOKEN:COMPANY-ID[:SITE-ID]" resolvers.
# Placeholders: {token}, {email}, {company}, {site}. The Authorization header is sent as
# "Bearer <token>" regardless of the URL template.
# TABFLEET_AUTOMATIQ_URL=https://api.automatiq.com/v1/accounts?email={email}&company_id={company}&site_id={site}
